## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical design for multi-tenant Azure AI apps with data residency, cost controls, and human-in-the-loop guardrails. It emphasizes end-to-end data flow, governance, and observability in real production settings.

## Key Concepts
- Azure OpenAI Deployment patterns across regions
- API Management and Front Door for routing and auth
- Grounding using a versioned KB in Blob + Cognitive Search
- PII redaction with Text Analytics and policy checks
- Per-tenant budgets with Cosmos DB-backed state and escalation queues
- Data Lake auditing and rollback strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
async function maybeCallOpenAI(tenantId, tokensNext){
  const budget = await getBudget(tenantId);
  if(budget - tokensNext < 0) {
    await enqueueHumanReview(tenantId);
    throw new Error("Budget exceeded");
  }
  return callOpenAI(/* ... */);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate per-tenant data residency across regions?
- What testing strategy ensures budget gating and humane escalation stays responsive?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to apply privacy, governance, and cost-control patterns to Azure OpenAI usage in a practical, real-world context.

## Key Concepts
- API Management as gateway for OpenAI calls
- KB grounding with Azure Blob and Cognitive Search
- PII redaction via Text Analytics
- Per-tenant policy gates to block risky questions
- Data Lake auditing and telemetry to monitor usage

## Code Example
```javascript
// PII redaction sample using Azure Text Analytics
const { TextAnalyticsClient, AzureKeyCredential } = require("@azure/ai-text-analytics");
const client = new TextAnalyticsClient("<endpoint>", new AzureKeyCredential("<key>"));
async function redactPII(text){
  // simplistic placeholder: detect entities and replace with [REDACTED]
  const result = await client.recognizeEntities([ { id: "1", language: "en", text } ]);
  let redacted = text;
  for(const e of result[0]?.entities || []){
    if(["PhoneNumber","Email","URL"].includes(e.category)){
      redacted = redacted.replaceAll(e.text, "[REDACTED]");
    }
  }
  return redacted;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the per-tenant gate across tenants with different budgets?
- How would you version the KB and ensure retroactive grounding for older queries?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests NL2SQL grounding, RBAC enforcement, privacy controls, and explainability in a realistic Azure OpenAI setup.

## Key Concepts
- NL2SQL grounding to a versioned KB
- Tenant-scoped RBAC gating
- PII redaction in both prompts and results
- Explainable AI: SQL + execution plan
- Safe fallback when policies block access

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation sketch: authenticate, fetch KB, generate SQL, enforce guards
async function nl2sql(user, nlQuery) {
  const ctx = await authenticate(user);
  const kb = await fetchKB(ctx tenantId);
  const sql = await generateSQL(nlQuery, kb);
  const guarded = applyRBAC(sql, ctx);
  const redacted = redactPII(guarded, ctx);
  const explain = explainSQL(redacted);
  return { sql: redacted, explain };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test for cross-tenant data leakage?
- How would you handle schema drift in the KB and keep responses in sync?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design practical multi-tenant localization, content grounding, and integration of Azure services with OpenAI.

## Key Concepts
- Language detection and translation using Azure Text Analytics and Azure Translator
- Grounding OpenAI responses to a KB stored in Azure Blob and indexed by Cognitive Search
- Per-tenant locale settings for currency/date formatting
- Error handling and fallback
- APIM as gateway and request routing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation sketch for data flow
async function handleQuery(input, tenant){
  const lang = detectLang(input);
  const q = translate(input, 'en');
  const grounded = await queryOpenAI(q, tenant);
  const res = translate(grounded, lang, lang);
  return res;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test locale formatting across locales?
- How would you handle translation latency and partial failures?
